WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.510
I'll break you into a thousand pieces!

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.560
I know that damaged him.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.010
<i>What a surprise...</i>

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:05.880
<i>Even General True's Golem with six
ligaments had trouble handling that claymore.</i>

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.160
<i>The horsepower of that Golem's
ligaments are out of this world.</i>

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.670
Is it gonna come?

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.670
You bastard!

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:30.860
What?!

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.530
He's swinging around his lance?

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.320
Doesn't he know how to fight?

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:54.890
It's coming!

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.070
I need to turn to the side.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.530
Asshole!

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.020
<i>I can't damage him when he
uses that claymore as his shield.</i>

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.220
I can't do anything from so far away.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.100
How much ammo have I wasted on him already?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.690
I'm going to run out.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.170
Please give up.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.600
W-What?

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:56.970
Don't tell me...

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.070
S-Stay back!

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.310
I'll open the gate!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.830
A hard inner frame?

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.720
I'll give you another one!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.070
What... the...?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.120
Why the hell is he so strong?!

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.910
I-It took its distance again.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:03.950
T-This is bad.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.840
He took my arm.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.950
I can't get close anymore.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.040
Damn!

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:24.950
I can do it!

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.140
Rygart?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.630
Are you okay?

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.340
Y-Yeah.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.570
Who are you?

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:03.880
Are you okay?

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.860
Oh, right.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.870
You can't speak through the quartz microphone.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.020
I am Dan and I serve General Baldr.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.350
I came to save you under his orders.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.030
H-Hey, wait!

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.510
What are you doing?!

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.420
You don't need to kill him!

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.900
Let me go!

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:36.460
We're in the middle of an operation
and we can't afford to take a prisoner.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.650
It's not showing any signs of surrendering either.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:41.660
Enemy backup could also be hiding somewhere nearby!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.180
We must exterminate the threat and continue moving.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.460
I understand that!

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.300
I-I know!

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.580
Let's just abandon this here!

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.570
This is armed!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.130
Do you want to be hit from behind?!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.210
Surrender, you asshole!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.580
You barbarians...

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.740
Huh?

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.430
You fucking barbarians!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.730
Barbarians?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.830
What's she talking about?

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.800
I'd rather die than be humiliated!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.560
H-Hey!

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:21.070
Zess...

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:24.050
It was an honor to have fought alongside you.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:24.970
Wait!

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:25.930
Hold on a minute!

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:31.930
Cleo, I think you should retire early.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:38.940
I don't care what you say.
You're not cut out to be a soldier.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:41.430
Stop! Don't do it!

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:31.230
They're much faster and have a much wider range...

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.840
We'll be at a geographical
disadvantage if we keep moving forward.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.290
Let's retreat to the meeting spot.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:42.240
Yes, sir.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.770
I think we could hold out a little longer.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.250
Are you worried about the other three?

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.770
I'm more than happy that we took down seven.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.770
And I never like splitting up a platoon.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.360
How's Dan?!

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.300
I'm gonna fall!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.060
You won't.

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.890
You will if I let go.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.320
Lee's late...

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.280
Lee's way too late.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:36.670
We retreated while under fire from the enemy,
so I don't think Cleo saw...

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:43.260
But from afar, I saw the black
Golem's lance shatter Lee's Artemis.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.200
How can that be...?

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:53.030
<i>I lost one of my subordinates because I let him go.</i>

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.330
I've made my decision.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:15.900
I'll surrender.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:21.380
Your Highness, as incompetent as I may be, I'd like to say...

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:24.050
that I do not approve.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.430
All my subordinates still wish to fight.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.840
Please give us another chance.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.840
What are you up to?

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:43.130
I received orders from Queen Sigyn to decipher the ancient language.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:46.360
This is one of the original parts of the Under Golem, right?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.850
Yeah, these writings were etched on the chest armor.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.750
I assume the ancients etched them in.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.560
I must say, I was surprised by this unit's capabilities.

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:04.010
But I heard it's going to be demolished since
it can't move anymore. It didn't even get named yet.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.620
Barbarians, huh?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:13.770
I was taught that both sides did cruel things
during the independence war 80 years ago, but...

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:19.710
I wonder if the education in Athens is more biased?

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:23.900
The soldier in that unit was young...

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:29.900
The girl we just buried was probably around 15 or 16—

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.010
Stop, I don't wanna hear it!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:33.650
I'm sorry!

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.960
Oh, no.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.060
Sorry, don't mind me.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.750
Let's switch, Erekt.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:52.840
I can't make the captain do the look out.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.210
Goodness Cleo...

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.840
She abandoned her one and only job.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.070
Is she still blue?

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:04.140
Lee and Cleo were from the same school.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.970
I heard Lee was an honors student

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:12.480
who always dragged Cleo to class
because all she did was tell fortunes.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.070
All because of my error...

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.780
Captain Zess, your strategy was flawless.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.900
Lee is the one who made the error.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.160
Dying is a part of a soldier's job.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.930
You're being too soft on those two.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:33.460
I understand that, but I also have a two year-old daughter.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.640
When I picture her going out to war one day,

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:41.020
I just can't help but treat them softly.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.610
I have always wanted to ask you...

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.660
I understand Lee, but why did you approve of Cleo's enlistment?

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:57.520
You know how most of the generals disapprove
of the Artemis for being a defective Golem?

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.140
That's rather off-topic.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:05.880
I wouldn't say it's defective, but it's more
stressful to control than any other Golem.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.360
Erekt, how long did it take you to get used to it?

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:11.730
A month, I'd say.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.600
Lee and Argath took two months.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.920
It took even me a week to get used to it.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.270
A week?!

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.630
I'm impressed.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.030
Cleo...

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.420
did it in a day.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:46.140
Rygart, after breakfast, can you come to the hang—

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:55.200
Sorry.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:59.410
I don't think I can do anything even if I'm here.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.210
I'm going home.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:06.840
Good luck.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.110
<i>Good bye, Rygart.</i>

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.630
<i>I'm glad to have seen you again before I die.</i>

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:00.840
Did you know Dan from work?

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:03.150
Y-Yeah, something like that.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:04.880
I'm his wife.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:08.460
I just can't believe it...

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:13.390
A Golem pilot's corpse isn't
allowed to be shown to non-personnel.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.430
I feel as if he's still...

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:20.020
Please take your time.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.790
I'm sure he'll love the company.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:36.470
Well, you can be mad at me all you want,

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:40.840
but at least you're lucky enough to have a kid on the way.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:44.740
My brother and I never get any girls.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:52.680
You must feel sort of responsible since you're here.

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.040
Responsible?

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:03.810
I just came here to give my prayers
to the idiot who showed up and died.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.910
You're just as His Highness said.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:09.960
You become dishonest with yourself when you feel hurt.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.950
He also told me about your father.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.380
He was disappointed to learn that you were an unsorcerer,

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:20.710
but he had sold all of his magical devices by the next day

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:24.880
and tried to show you how to work in the fields with two arms and legs.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:32.010
You always speak ill of your father,
but you actually respect him.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:33.680
That's what His Highness told me.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.280
In any case, Dan's death isn't anyone's fault.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.280
Sadly, it was caused by his lack of judgment.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.020
Don't worry about it.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.990
I'm not worried about it!

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:44.940
Don't make me repeat myself!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.170
See ya.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:51.940
Rygart.

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:54.950
What do you want? I'm done here.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.000
I'd like you to participate in the next sortie.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.250
Sortie?

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.740
Yeah, right! That has nothing to do with me.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.750
Even if His Highness has decided to surrender?

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:08.460
<i>Athens has proposed a peace treaty.</i>

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.920
<i>The execution of the Krisnan Royal Family.</i>

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.520
I do feel bad for Hodr, but...

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:19.730
But I...!

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:25.730
Queen Sigyn believes that ancient Under Golem can still operate.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.730
Only you are capable of moving that.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.730
Please fight alongside us, Rygart.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.360
I...

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:42.650
I was just coincidentally born in
the countryside of Krisna and I'm...

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:45.640
I will not let His Highness be beheaded in Athens—

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:55.880
Shut up!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.540
If you're going home,
you should've said something to me.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:21.540
Sorry.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.900
Don't make that face.

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.210
I didn't come to stop you.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:30.500
If I had known they'd be
coming for the capital so quickly,

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:32.300
I wouldn't have called you here.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.450
I thought I had more time to talk.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.080
Oh yeah, here.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.340
What's that?

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.970
Well, a parting gift.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:46.070
Please take it.

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:48.560
It's not like the money from back then.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.580
Back then?

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.060
You don't remember?

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:55.080
Well, it has been five years...

00:19:55.450 --> 00:20:00.080
You know that time you said you were
going to quit school because you couldn't pay,

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:04.360
and I told you that I could ask my
father to do something about it?

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.840
You got really mad.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:11.290
My dad taught me to never borrow money from a friend!

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.000
Even if I'm being chased by loan sharks!

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.140
Oh...

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:17.500
Did I?

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.110
That's embarrassing.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.600
I was ashamed for being so thoughtless,

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.110
but it made me happy.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.270
Farewell, Rygart.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:31.710
Till we meet again.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.920
<i>Hodr knew...</i>

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.620
<i>He knew that we'd never meet again.</i>

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.000
I'm so happy to see you.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:55.900
He picked a fight with destiny.

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:58.760
I'd say he's an admirable father.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.780
I couldn't fight it.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:05.210
It's the same writing as the one on the Golem's chest.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:11.730
The words the ancients went out of their way to etch...

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:15.420
"Let us fight destiny."

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:21.220
Rygart...

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.180
Rygart.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:31.500
There's nothing shameful about running away.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:35.600
Some things are just out of people's hands.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:39.990
If you think you're gonna die, just run.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.730
What are you doing, Rygart?

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:03.990
<i>Sorry, Dad.</i>

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:53.810
What I'm I doing? Holding back against Zess?!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:58.930
Counterattack, violent retaliation.
